## Commands
- **Prepare Dependencies:** `just setup`
- **Build Local Binary:** `just build` (compiles to `bin/{{.Binary}}`)
- **Run CLI with Arguments:** `just run [args...]`
- **Run CLI in Agent Mode:** `just run-ai [args...]` (`AGENT=1`)
- **Run Tests:** `just test` (`go test -race -cover ./...`)
- **Run Static Analysis & Tests:** `just check`
- **Run Linter / Static Analysis:** `just vet` or `just lint` (`go mod tidy -diff` and `go vet ./...`)
- **Format Source Code:** `just fmt` (`go fmt ./...`)

## Setup & Environment
- **Prerequisites:** Go {{.GoVersion}}+, `just`.
- **Development Storage:** Use a unique, task-owned child of the project's ignored `.tmp/` for disposable development scratch. Point `TMPDIR` and `GOTMPDIR` at that child and remove only that child when its last consumer finishes, including on failure or cancellation. Never wipe `.tmp/` or another task's files. Keep regenerable caches in ignored `.cache/` and retained state, locks, queues, logs, and reports in ignored `.state/`; files that must outlive the session do not belong in `.tmp/`. `just clean` removes build and coverage outputs and preserves these storage directories.

## Conventions
- **Output Formatting & No Decorative Headers:** All CLI output must be plain text without emojis across all modes.
- **Help Screens & Terminal Width:** Help must use `github.com/alexgorbatchev/cobra-help-tree/v4` through `SetupWithOptions`, with positional arguments and environment variables documented in `techCatalog`. Help renders an aligned hierarchical tree view with `├─` and `╰─` glyphs, with long help text wrapped to the terminal width and never truncated.
- **Agent Mode (`AGENT=1`):** When `AGENT=1` is set, output compact key-value pairs or bullets. Use `cobrahelptree.IsAgentMode`.
- **Errors:** `run` in `cmd/{{.Binary}}/main.go` prints every command error once, as `[ERROR]` for people and `ERR:` for agents. Keep `SilenceErrors` and `SilenceUsage` set on the root command.
- **Hermetic Unit Tests:** All unit tests must remain 100% offline and hermetic.

## Agent Skill
- The skill lives only at `skills/{{.Binary}}/SKILL.md` at the repository root. Never embed it in the binary or keep a second copy.
- `{{.Binary}} skill` prints install instructions through `HelpOptions.Skill`, and every agent help screen starts with an alert to read it.
- Update the skill in the same change as any command, argument, flag, shorthand, type, default, accepted value, environment variable, output, error, or side-effect change. Include generated help and completion commands. Verify it against the implementation and pinned dependencies, update `last_modified`, and run `just check`. `TestSkillDocumentsCommandInterface` compares it with the live command tree through `cobrahelptree.SkillOmissions`.
- Write affirmative usage instructions and factual contracts in the skill. Keep development instructions and prohibitions in this file.
- Do not use the usage skill for developing the Go implementation, or invent unsupported operations.

## Boundaries
- **Always:** For code changes that alter executable behavior, add or update meaningful behavioral tests. Require at least 90% line coverage and 90% function coverage across the non-test source of each affected first-party package, including unexecuted files and excluding `scripts/` directories. Measure with `go test -coverprofile`. Do not weaken coverage gates or make token test edits.
- **Always:** Run `just check` before committing changes.
- **Always:** Persist standing project instructions in this file and update the relevant rule in place.
- **Never:** Record task history, progress, handoffs, or dated user amendments in `AGENTS.md`.
- **Never:** Commit compiled Go binaries (e.g. `bin/{{.Binary}}`) to git.
- **Never:** Publish releases, tags, packages, or production deployments automatically without explicit user authorization.
